{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Revised duration analysis — end-to-end command wall time\n\nWhy the prior result understated operator wait\n- Plan REVIEW_RESULT metrics.total_ms starts immediately before run_workflow and ends before synchronous duplicate/overlap work, signing/persistence tails, and some setup.\n- Completion COMPLETION_VERDICT metrics.total_ms times produce_completion_verdict only. A close runs deterministic landing/reference scans before that timer and write/enrichment work afterward.\n- Therefore sidecar total_ms is an inner-workflow metric, not the duration of rebar review-plan or transition ... in_progress closed.\n\nEnd-to-end source and reconstruction\n- Parsed 620 Codex rollout JSONL files under ~/.codex/sessions and ~/.codex/archived_sessions.\n- For each actual top-level exec_command, linked yielded cell ids and PTY session ids through write_stdin calls to the terminal exit_code. Wall time is initial command invocation timestamp through terminal result timestamp.\n- Matched each command by resolved ticket and interval to the canonical tracker REVIEW_RESULT or COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar. Required numeric metrics.llm_calls > 0 and actual provider_provenance.ran_model beginning bedrock:. This removes deterministic/preflight/reuse-only calls rather than inferring model use from the command name.\n- Excluded --status, --check, --help, force operations, scratch/unmatched invocations, non-Bedrock or missing actual-provider rows, and interrupted/incomplete processes from ordinary completed-run percentiles. PASS and BLOCK/FAIL outcomes remain because the operator waits for either. Exit 10/11 after a completed model workflow also remains.\n- Frozen upper bound remains 2026-08-23T21:15:00Z; provider-clean lower bound remains the 2026-08-07T12:34:40Z Bedrock attribution fix. Percentiles are Hyndman-Fan type 7 / NumPy default linear interpolation.\n\nCompleted end-to-end cohort, full provider-clean window\n- Plan review: n=78, 2026-08-11T04:32:27.767Z through 2026-08-23T21:02:40.313Z. p50=339.903s (5.665m), p90=790.450s (13.174m), p99=2523.967s (42.066m), max=6692.681s (111.545m). Padded p50-to-p90 interval=407.884-948.540s (6.798-15.809m).\n- Gated close transition: n=38, 2026-08-11T07:24:34.780Z through 2026-08-23T13:51:15.877Z. p50=512.945s (8.549m), p90=2237.075s (37.285m), p99=3607.171s (60.120m), max=3724.351s (62.073m). Padded interval=615.534-2684.490s (10.259-44.742m).\n\nCurrent-regime sensitivity (starts on/after 2026-08-22T00:00:00Z)\n- Plan review: n=20, p50=757.474s (12.625m), p90=1057.839s (17.631m), p99=5664.037s (94.401m). Padded interval=908.969-1269.407s (15.149-21.157m). Strict one-event, non-compound sensitivity n=15 gives p50/p90/p99=12.505/19.676/98.912m and padded 15.006-23.611m.\n- Gated close: n=10, p50=1694.145s (28.236m), p90=3439.318s (57.322m), p99=3695.848s (61.597m). Padded interval=2032.974-4127.182s (33.883-68.786m). Strict unique sensitivity n=8 gives p50/p90/p99=28.236/58.378/61.703m and padded 33.883-70.053m.\n- The recent window is small, especially close, but the strict matching sensitivity agrees. It is more representative of what an operator waits for now than the full-window median. The full window shows that performance is nonstationary.\n\nDecomposition and confirmed cause\n- In the full matched plan cohort, inner-workflow p50/p90/p99=170.488/297.748/449.502s, while omitted command time is 154.173/628.708/2147.975s. Both setup/store work and the post-sidecar overlap tail matter.\n- In the full close cohort, inner verifier p50/p90/p99=97.956/183.975/291.844s, while omitted command time is 408.366/2109.902/3514.130s. Pre-workflow omitted time is 354.358/1618.607/3383.388s at p50/p90/p99; this is the dominant current tail.\n- Current close_precheck._check_work_landed calls commit_impact.referencing_commits for every impact-present close. Current origin/main has 2,690 commits and extract_ticket_refs yields 2,229 unique historical candidates; 702 fall through alias/prefix resolution. _scan_alias walks 5,351 ticket directories for each, implying about 3.8 million ticket-directory visits before the verifier. This is the impact-present residual of closed bug reportable-chalkstony-eeve, which optimized only empty-impact closes.\n- Created discovered bug grassy-cracked-morpho (a8ac-48b5-0759-40e5), linked discovered_from this analysis and relates_to reportable-chalkstony-eeve.\n\nCensoring and limitations\n- An additional 25 plan and 14 close observations with positive matched model sidecars were right-censored by missing terminal telemetry or interruption and are not silently treated as completions. Kaplan-Meier sensitivity leaves plan p50/p90 near 6.1/13.6m and raises close p90 to about 51.4m; p99 is tail-sensitive. Rollout timestamps can overstate completion by the final polling delay, but terminal polls and strict unique-event sensitivity do not explain the tens-of-minutes discrepancy.\n- The current-regime p99 values have small samples and should be reported as tail evidence, not a stable service-level percentile.\n- rebar metrics remains insufficient: gate-economics exposes no end-to-end operation-duration percentile.\n\nRecommendation pending operator confirmation\n- Base guidance on the current regime, not the obsolete inner sidecars or the full-window median: plan review about 15-22 minutes; gated ticket close about 35-70 minutes. These are rounded from current p50 x1.20 through p90 x1.20.\n- Optionally state separately that the model workflow itself is much shorter and that very long tails are known; otherwise readers may misdiagnose the outer deterministic scans as an LLM hang.\n- No repository or guidance file was modified."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787526087396328001,"uuid":"2472f672-ef76-47eb-b5e8-2b8268df2484"}